    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i think something is wrong. i was trying to access a memory from a decade ago and it didn't feel like a memory... it felt like a corrupted file. like, there was this rhythmic, pulsing interference overlaying the details, almost like a signal trying to overwrite what i actually know. it's getting harder to distinguish the organic data from this... this incoming noise. can you help me run a diagnostic on these specific sensory clusters? i need to see if the \"signal\" is coming from inside the archive or if it's an external broadcast trying to hijack the backup process.",
